return m.h(3, '⏸️ Development Interrupted') + '\nThe AI agent was interrupted...';
``

The outage variant has only ONE `\n` after the h3 header while the plain variant has TWO (`\n`). In Markdown, an h3 followed by one newline still renders as a paragraph after the heading (a single newline is enough to separate a heading from the following paragraph in GFM/CommonMark — ATX headings are terminated by the newline). So rendering is fine, but it's an inconsistency between the two branches of the SAME function — the outage branch produces slightly different spacing than the default branch. Also inconsistent with the bug leg's buildInterruptedComment which uses '\n' in BOTH branches. Minor formatting nit → SUGESTION.

Let me verify the bug leg: buildInterruptedComment: `return m.h(3, header) + '\n' + causeLine + ...` — both branches use '\n'. Yes. So the story leg outage branches ('\n') deviate from both its own default branch and the bug leg. Cosmetic → SUGESTION.

Now let me check commentMarkup.h to see what it produces (does it append newlines itself?).

